tml\",\"settings\":{\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"wf-eyebrow-wrap\\\"><span class=\\\"wf-eyebrow\\\">Our mission<\\/span><\\/p>\"},\"elements\":[]},{\"id\":\"6e58cb5\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"heading\",\"settings\":{\"title\":\"Make good work easy to find \\u2014 on both sides of the brief\",\"header_size\":\"h2\",\"typography_typography\":\"custom\",\"typography_font_size\":{\"unit\":\"px\",\"size\":38},\"typography_font_weight\":\"700\",\"typography_line_height\":{\"unit\":\"em\",\"size\":1.2},\"typography_letter_spacing\":{\"unit\":\"px\",\"size\":-0.4}},\"elements\":[]},{\"id\":\"3690037\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"widgetType\":\"text-editor\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<p>Hiring a specialist should not feel like a gamble, and finding good work should not mean bidding against fifty people for the lowest price. Those two problems are the same problem viewed from opposite ends, and Workfoster exists to close the gap between them.<\\/p>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<p>We do that by doing the unglamorous parts properly: interviewing every specialist before they appear in a shortlist, writing briefs that say what success actually looks like, and holding money in escrow so neither side is exposed.<\\/p>\",\"typography_typography\":\"custom\",\"typography_font_size\":{\"unit\":\"px\",\"size\":16.5},\"typography_line_height\":{\"unit\":\"em\",\"size\":1.75},\"text_color\":\"#47584F\"},\"elements\":[]}],\"isInner\":false},{\"id\":\"a6ff14c\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":{\"content_width\":\"full\",\"width\":{\"unit\":\"%\",\"size\":54},\"width_tablet\":{\"unit\":\"%\",\"size\":100},\"width_mobile\":{\"unit\":\"%\",\"size\":100},\"flex_direction\":\"column\",\"flex_gap\":{\"unit\":\"px\",\"size\":18,\"column\":\"18\",\"row\":\"18\",\"isLinked\":true},\"padding\":{\"unit\":\"px\",\"top\":\"0\",\"right\":\"0\",\"bottom\":\"0\",\"left\":\"0\",\"isLinked\":false}},\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"54d1e72\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":{\"content_width\":\"full\",\"widt